1
00:04:27,500 --> 00:04:33,500
Music is a music, drama film directed by Sia.

2
00:08:55,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Zu, a free spirit estranged from her family, suddenly finds herself the sole guardian of her half-sister, Music, a
teenager on the autism spectrum whose whole world order has been beautifully crafted by her late grandmother.

3
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:28,500
The film soon challenges whether it is Zu or Music who has a better view of the world, and
that love, trust, and being able to be there for each other is everything.

4
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Zu, played by Kate Hudson.

5
00:22:17,500 --> 00:22:23,500
Ebo, played by Leslie Odom Jr..

6
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:51,000
Music, played by Maddie Ziegler.

7
00:31:12,500 --> 00:31:18,500
Millie, played by Mary Kay Place.

8
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:46,000
Felix, played by Beto Calvillo.

9
00:40:07,500 --> 00:40:13,500
Evelyn, played by Juliette Lewis.

10
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:41,000
Music is a 2021 American musical drama film directed by singer-songwriter Sia.

11
00:49:02,500 --> 00:49:08,500
The film was co-written by Sia and Dallas Clayton,
and stars Kate Hudson, Leslie Odom Jr.

12
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:36,000
and Maddie Ziegler.

13
00:57:57,500 --> 00:58:03,500
It marks Sia's feature film directorial debut.

14
01:02:25,000 --> 01:02:31,000
The film follows Zu, a newly sober drug dealer who becomes the sole guardian
of her half-sister Music, a teenage non-verbal autistic girl.

15
01:06:52,500 --> 01:06:58,500
The film began development following Sia's announcement of the project in 2015.

16
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
Originally intended as a non-musical film, it was subsequently re-conceived as
a musical with a larger budget, and was filmed in mid-2017.

17
01:15:47,500 --> 01:15:53,500
A studio album by Sia was also released in connection with the
film, including some of the 10 songs she wrote for it.

18
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:21,000
Music was released in Australia on January 14, 2021, by StudioCanal, and in select IMAX theatres in the United States for one
night on February 10, 2021, followed by an on-demand release on February 12, 2021, by Vertical Entertainment.

19
01:24:42,500 --> 01:24:48,500
The film was a box office failure, grossing
$645,949 against its $16 million budget.

20
01:29:10,000 --> 01:29:16,000
Music received generally negative reviews from critics, with most
criticism stemming from its depiction of autism.

21
01:33:37,500 --> 01:33:43,500
It was nominated for Best Motion Picture – Musical or Comedy and Best Actress – Motion Picture Comedy or Musical (Hudson) at the 78th Golden Globe Awards, but was
also nominated for four Golden Raspberry Awards, winning Worst Actress for Hudson, Worst Supporting Actress for Ziegler and Worst Director for Sia.

22
01:38:05,000 --> 01:38:11,000
The film explores themes of drug dealer, autism,
macabre, celebratory, disrespectful.

23
01:42:32,500 --> 01:42:38,500
The tone is emotional.
